---
// Keyholders — an unlisted page for people Russ invites. Not in the nav or sitemap.
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>For our Keyholders — Vault Human</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <meta name="description" content="An invitation to see what Vault Human is building, and to walk it with us." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="For our Keyholders — Vault Human" /><meta property="og:description" content="A coach every day. For the whole of you. An invitation to see what we are building." /><meta property="og:image" content="https://www.vaulthuman.com/og-vaulthuman.png" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&family=Fraunces:ital,wght@0,400;1,400&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=AW-18371546487"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];window.gtag=function(){dataLayer.push(arguments);};var gtag=window.gtag;
    gtag('js',new Date());gtag('config','AW-18371546487');gtag('config','G-B2NDY58EKD');
  </script>
  <style is:inline>
    *{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
    :root{--bg:#101511;--bg2:#141a16;--card:#171e19;--line:#263028;--ink:#EDEBE4;--soft:#c9cdc6;--mute:#8f988f;--sage:#8FA67E;--past:#D2A576;--now:#9DC0DE;--fut:#A9C397}
    html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
    body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;line-height:1.6}
    img{display:block;max-width:100%}
    a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
    .wrap{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}
    section{padding:96px 0}
    .alt{background:var(--bg2)}
    .eyebrow{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:4px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sage);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:14px}
    h1,h2{font-family:'Bebas Neue',sans-serif;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.5px;line-height:.95}
    h1{font-size:clamp(56px,9vw,112px)}
    h2{font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,66px);margin-bottom:18px}
    h3{font-family:'Bebas Neue',sans-serif;font-weight:400;font-size:26px;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:6px}
    p{font-size:16px;color:var(--soft)}
    .lede{font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--ink);max-width:760px}
    .serif{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-style:italic}
    .bar{height:3px;width:64px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--sage);margin:24px 0}
    .grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}
    .grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px}
    .grid4{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:18px}
    .card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:22px}
    .card p{font-size:15px}
    .num{font-family:'Bebas Neue';font-size:54px;color:var(--sage);line-height:1}
    .tile{border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card)}
    .tile .ph{aspect-ratio:4/3;background-size:cover;background-position:center 25%}
    .tile .t{padding:18px 20px}
    .tile .t p{font-size:14.5px}
    .hero{position:relative;min-height:92vh;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:0 0 80px;background:url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?w=2000&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop) center/cover}
    .hero:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(10,13,11,.2) 0%,rgba(10,13,11,.5) 45%,rgba(10,13,11,.97) 100%)}
    .hero .wrap{position:relative;z-index:2}
    .topbar{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:3;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:28px 24px;max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto}
    .brand{font-family:'Bebas Neue';font-size:24px;letter-spacing:6px}
    .brand b{color:var(--sage);font-weight:400}
    .topbar a.site{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:3px;color:var(--soft)}
    .letter{display:grid;grid-template-columns:300px 1fr;gap:56px;align-items:start}
    .letter img{border-radius:12px;width:100%}
    .letter p{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:18px}
    .why{position:relative;background:url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511632765486-a01980e01a18?w=2000&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop) center 35%/cover}
    .why:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(16,21,17,.35),rgba(16,21,17,.97) 65%)}
    .why .wrap{position:relative;z-index:2;padding-top:30vh}
    table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px}
    th{text-align:left;font-weight:600;color:var(--sage);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #2c352e}
    td{padding:13px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #222a24;color:var(--soft);vertical-align:top}
    td b{color:var(--ink)}
    .cap{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--mute);margin-top:10px;line-height:1.4}
    .phone{border-radius:22px;border:2px solid var(--line);overflow:hidden}
    .svgw svg{width:100%;height:auto}
    .coachgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1fr;grid-template-rows:240px 240px;gap:14px}
    .coachgrid > div{border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;position:relative}
    .coachgrid img,.coachgrid video{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 25%}
    .coachgrid .big{grid-row:1/3}
    .vid{position:relative;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;background:#000;aspect-ratio:16/9}
    .vid video{width:100%;height:100%;display:block}
    .fine{padding:120px 0 60px}
    .fine p{font-size:12px;color:var(--mute);max-width:820px;line-height:1.6}
    .step{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:flex-start}
    .step .num{font-size:40px;min-width:40px}
    .wheelrow{grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}
    @media (max-width:860px){
      section{padding:72px 0}
      .grid2,.grid3,.grid4{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
      .letter{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .letter img{max-width:260px}
      .coachgrid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-template-rows:260px 180px 180px}
      .coachgrid .big{grid-column:1/3;grid-row:1}
      .hero{min-height:80vh}
    }
    @media (max-width:560px){
      .grid2,.grid3,.grid4{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .coachgrid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-template-rows:220px 150px 150px}
      .wheelrow{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .phone{max-width:240px!important}
      h2{font-size:44px}
      .lede{font-size:18px}
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="/">VAULT <b>HUMAN</b></a><a class="site" href="https://www.vaulthuman.com/">VAULTHUMAN.COM</a></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">For our Keyholders</p>
    <h1>A coach every day.<br><span style="color:var(--sage)">For the whole of you.</span></h1>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="serif" style="font-size:24px;color:var(--ink);max-width:640px">An invitation to see what we are building, and to walk it with us.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="letter">
  <div class="wrap letter">
    <div>
      <img src="/russ-michaels.jpg" alt="Russ Michaels" />
      <p class="cap">Russ Michaels<br>Founder, Vault Human</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A letter</p>
      <h2>Dear Keyholder,</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink)">Thank you for opening this. Before I show you anything, I want you to know why it exists.</p>
      <p>Most of us were handed the pieces of ourselves, never the whole. A little advice here, a lesson there, a hard season we walked through alone. We learned to get by. Very few of us were ever taught how to grow on purpose, a day at a time, with someone in our corner.</p>
      <p>I have spent more than twenty years leading organizations and sitting with people in the moments that shape them. What I have seen, over and over, is that people are far bigger than the stories they have been told about themselves. When someone feels heard, seen and believed in, they rise. Almost always.</p>
      <p>Vault Human is my answer to that. Each morning, a short key arrives: something to learn, something to love, something to live. You take one small step. You write down what you notice. A coach walks beside you. Over a year, it comes full circle, and you come home to more of yourself.</p>
      <p>And here is the part that moves me most. When one person grows, everyone who loves them feels it. A mother who finally feels heard. A teenager who learns early that his voice matters. A father who finds his footing again. A team that starts telling each other the truth. That is how the world gets kinder: one person, one day, one key at a time.</p>
      <p>You are receiving this because you are someone I trust to see it early. I would love for you to walk it with us.</p>
      <p class="serif" style="font-size:24px;color:var(--ink);margin-top:28px">With gratitude,<br>Russ</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why we exist</p>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(48px,7vw,92px)">Big, not small.<br><span style="color:var(--sage)">Empowered, not disempowered.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">We believe every person carries more than they have been told. Vault Human exists to help people grow into it, and to finish each day a little more of who they are.</p>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:40px">
      <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid var(--past)"><h3 style="color:var(--past)">Seen</h3><p>Your past honored, not erased. What shaped you becomes something you can work with.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid var(--now)"><h3 style="color:var(--now)">Heard</h3><p>Your voice in the present, all the way to the end of what you have to say.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid var(--fut)"><h3 style="color:var(--fut)">Empowered</h3><p>Your future, chosen on purpose and lived into, one day at a time.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="who">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
    <h2>Life does not wait<br>until we are ready.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Picture the people you love. One of them is carrying something right now.</p>
    <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:36px">
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="background-image:url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1475609471617-0ef53b59cff5?w=1000&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop);background-position:center 18%"></div><div class="t"><h3>The mother</h3><p>She gives all day and goes to bed last. Ten quiet minutes each morning become the one place where someone asks how <i>she</i> is, and listens.</p></div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="background-image:url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758272959140-e727ef77bbda?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop);background-position:center 30%"></div><div class="t"><h3>The teenager</h3><p>Sixteen, and the world is loud. A daily key teaches him to notice his own mind, to speak up, and to trust that he is more than a screen says he is.</p></div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="background-image:url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1616587894289-86480e533129?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop);background-position:center 30%"></div><div class="t"><h3>The father</h3><p>Steady for everyone else, unsure inside. A coach on a call, a page to write on, and a path that does not ask him to have it all figured out.</p></div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="background-image:url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1752659504423-87916d12bc37?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop);background-position:center 30%"></div><div class="t"><h3>The team</h3><p>Talented people, talking past each other. When a team walks the same keys together, they start listening, and the work gets lighter.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="alt" id="get-1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What you get · one</p>
    <h2>You get your life back.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Your past, your present and your future, held together instead of in pieces. That is the whole idea of the Vault Approach: one year that moves through all three, so you can see where you came from, stand where you are, and choose where you are going.</p>
    <div class="svgw" style="margin:36px 0 28px;max-width:760px"><svg viewBox="0 0 680 88" width="680" height="88"><polygon points="0.0,0 200.66666666666666,0 218.66666666666666,26 200.66666666666666,52 0.0,52 0.0,26" fill="#D2A576" fill-opacity="0.16" stroke="#D2A576" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="109.33333333333333" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bebas Neue" font-size="17" letter-spacing="2" fill="#D2A576">PAST</text><text x="109.33333333333333" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter" font-size="11" fill="#dfe3dc">Learn · as learned</text><polygon points="230.66666666666666,0 431.3333333333333,0 449.3333333333333,26 431.3333333333333,52 230.66666666666666,52 248.66666666666666,26" fill="#9DC0DE" fill-opacity="0.16" stroke="#9DC0DE" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="340.0" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bebas Neue" font-size="17" letter-spacing="2" fill="#9DC0DE">PRESENT</text><text x="340.0" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter" font-size="11" fill="#dfe3dc">Love · as loved</text><polygon points="461.3333333333333,0 662.0,0 680.0,26 662.0,52 461.3333333333333,52 479.3333333333333,26" fill="#A9C397" fill-opacity="0.16" stroke="#A9C397" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="570.6666666666666" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bebas Neue" font-size="17" letter-spacing="2" fill="#A9C397">FUTURE</text><text x="570.6666666666666" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter" font-size="11" fill="#dfe3dc">Live · as lived</text><rect x="0" y="62" width="680" height="22" rx="11" fill="none" stroke="#8FA67E" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/><text x="340.0" y="77" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter" font-size="10.5" letter-spacing="3" fill="#8FA67E">LISTEN · ALL YEAR · AS HEARD, AS DISCERNED, AS CREATED</text></svg></div>
    <div class="grid2 wheelrow">
      <img src="/img/keyholders/wheel.png" alt="The Vault Approach wheel: one year, eleven chambers, nine gates" style="border-radius:14px" />
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:30px">One year. Eleven chambers. Nine gates.</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px">The year moves through eleven chambers, one part of your life at a time. Along the way are nine gates, and each one opens when a daily practice stops being something you try and becomes something you live.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px">You begin with yourself, honor what shaped you, rest in the middle, and finish by giving something back. Gates, not dates: nothing is due on anyone else's clock.</p>
        <p class="serif" style="color:var(--ink);font-size:19px">Full circle. One year. The whole of you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="get-2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What you get · two</p>
    <h2>You get the keys.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Every chamber opens with keys: short teachings, each with one small practice. A key arrives each morning. You carry it through the day. When the practice holds, the key turns, and the gate opens.</p>
    <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:44px;align-items:center;gap:48px">
      <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center"><img class="phone" src="/img/inside/letter.jpg" alt="The morning letter, Who Made You, on a phone" style="max-width:300px" /></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Your first key</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:40px">Who made you.</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:14px;color:var(--ink);font-size:17px">Someone believed in you before you believed in yourself. Maybe it was a teacher who kept you after class, a coach who wouldn't let you quit on a bad day, a boss who handed you the keys and walked out the door. Most of them never heard what it meant.</p>
        <p>That is the first key. A short morning letter, one small practice, and a week to carry it. Three moves: name them, write it down, read it to them. You are not the only one who changes when it's read out loud.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid4" style="margin-top:48px">
      <div><img src="/img/inside/booklet-cover.jpg" alt="" style="border-radius:10px" /><p class="cap">The booklet: a key you can hold</p></div>
      <div><img src="/img/inside/booklet-day1.jpg" alt="" style="border-radius:10px" /><p class="cap">Day one: the name</p></div>
      <div><img src="/img/inside/booklet-key.jpg" alt="" style="border-radius:10px" /><p class="cap">The teaching, in plain words</p></div>
      <div><img src="/img/inside/booklet-practice.jpg" alt="" style="border-radius:10px" /><p class="cap">Three moves, one week</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="alt" id="get-3">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What you get · three</p>
    <h2>You get the tools,<br>and a coach.</h2>
    <p class="lede">A letter every morning. A booklet for every key. An app that captures your work, any hour, from anywhere in the world. And a real person in your corner.</p>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:40px">
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="aspect-ratio:3/4;background-image:url(/img/inside/letter.jpg);background-position:center top"></div><div class="t"><h3>The letter</h3><p>Every morning, in your inbox and your app. One teaching, one practice.</p></div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="aspect-ratio:3/4;background-image:url(/img/inside/booklet-cover.jpg);background-position:center top"></div><div class="t"><h3>The booklet</h3><p>Each key as something you can hold, print and keep.</p></div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ph" style="aspect-ratio:3/4;background-image:url(/img/inside/app-capture.jpg);background-position:center top"></div><div class="t"><h3>The capture tool</h3><p>Write it, say it or snap it the moment it lands. A private folder that becomes your year in your own words.</p></div></div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:88px">
      <p class="eyebrow">The coach</p>
      <h2>A real person<br>in your corner.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Russ Michaels created Vault Human and coaches every member. More than twenty years leading organizations, more than ten as a chief executive and board president, more than ten as an attorney, and a decade in hospitality, where he learned that people wait patiently when they know they have been seen.</p>
      <div class="coachgrid" style="margin-top:36px">
        <div class="big"><video autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="/img/russ/coach/coach-point.jpg" aria-label="Russ on stage"><source src="/img/russ/coach/coach-point.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video></div>
        <div><img src="/img/russ/strip/friend.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:center 30%" /></div>
        <div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565813086292-604790c8a97b?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="" style="object-position:center 35%" /></div>
        <div><img src="/img/russ/coach/coach-field.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:center 40%" /></div>
        <div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542323228-002ac256e7b8?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="" style="object-position:center 45%" /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:28px">
        <div class="card"><h3>Every member</h3><p>A live group call with Russ each month, recorded for anyone who cannot attend.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Circles</h3><p>Small groups of six who walk the chambers together, twice a month.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>One-on-one</h3><p>Three private sessions a month for those who want to go deeper.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="serif" style="font-size:19px;color:var(--ink);margin-top:28px;text-align:center">Coaching, not therapy. A person, not a program.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="membership">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The plan · why membership</p>
    <h2>Built on the<br><span style="color:var(--sage)">forever relationship.</span></h2>
    <p class="lede">The strongest personal-growth companies no longer sell one course at a time. They invite people into a membership and keep earning their trust, month after month. Robbie Kellman Baxter calls it "the forever transaction" in <i>The Membership Economy</i>.</p>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:36px">
      <div class="card"><div class="num">$51B</div><p>Global personal development market in 2025, projected near $80B by 2033 (Grand View Research).</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="num">122,974</div><p>Coaches worldwide, up 15% since 2023, in a $5.34B coaching industry (ICF Global Coaching Study, 2025).</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="num">11%</div><p>Faster revenue growth for subscription companies than the S&amp;P 500 over two years (Zuora Subscription Economy Index, 2025).</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:22px">
      <div class="card"><h3>Keeping members is the whole game</h3><p>Bain &amp; Company research by Frederick Reichheld found a 5% rise in retention lifts profit 25% to 95%. Keeping a member costs a fraction of finding a new one (Harvard Business Review, 2014).</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>The closest model: Mindvalley</h3><p>A global personal-growth membership: every program, community and author sessions for $99 a month or $499 a year, with a Pro tier that adds live sessions with its founder. Brendon Burchard's GrowthDay runs a similar daily-coaching membership.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:22px;border-left:3px solid var(--sage)"><p style="color:var(--ink)"><b>Where Vault Human is different:</b> a single guided year instead of a library to browse, a real coach inside every membership, and a capture tool that turns each day's practice into a record of who you are becoming.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="alt" id="paths">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The plan · how people arrive</p>
    <h2>Every path runs<br>through the membership.</h2>
    <p class="lede">However someone finds us, they begin as a member. Deeper coaching is added on top, and the membership keeps renewing underneath.</p>
